/// A code point outside the Basic Multilingual Plane is still one Char.
///
/// Separate from StringCodePoints because the two fail apart.  An emoji is four
/// bytes in UTF-8 and two units in UTF-16, so a fix that counts UTF-16 units
/// rather than code points passes that file and fails this one -- reporting a
/// length of 2 where the answer is 1.
///
/// The quoted literal is a Char here rather than a String, since the rule is
/// one code point between the quotes and not one byte.
///
/// Fails with: Assertion 'left = right' failed.  Expected '1' but got '4'.
///
test 'An astral code point is one Char';
begin
    var Face : String := '😀';

    AssertEqual (1, Length (Face));
    AssertTrue  ('😀' is Char);
    AssertEqual (128512, Ord ('😀'));
    AssertEqual (3, Length ('a😀b'));
    AssertEqual (1, Pos ('a😀b', '😀'));
end
